\newlabel{fig:defense_tradeoff}{{4}{14}{Recovery-score reduction versus realized protected-payload overhead, averaged equally over the two 96-token pilot models ($n=30$ prompts each; up to three segments, three samples per segment, 80-token T5 input and output limits). Both coordinates use the completed runs. Batching has zero payload-sum overhead and changes the frame count; latency was not measured. These are pipeline scores, not information-theoretic privacy estimates.\relax }{figure.caption.14}{}}
